Lab: User ID controlled by request parameter, with unpredictable user IDs 

Goal:- Lab has a horizontal privilege escalation vulnerability on the user account page, but identifies users with GUIDs. To solve the lab, find the GUID for carlos, then submit his API key as the solution. 

Observation:- Disclosre of user ids in URL where we can access the info of the account of other users

Steps to solve :- 

        Step1:- Access the lab
        Step2:- Login using given credentials
        Step3:- Go to Home
        step4:- Open any vlog 
        Step5:- click on the user and there exist a their GUIDs in the search bar
        Step6:- In my account replace that id with your GUID 
        Step7:- report the api to the server

Result:- Access to other user account by changing the GUID which is disclosed in view account

Root Cause:- The application uses GUID based identifiers but fails to implement proper server-side object level authorization, allowing users to access other accounts once valid GUIDs are discovered.

Fix:- Implement strict object level authorization on the server side and ensure that resource access is validated against the authenticated user, regardless of identifier type.
